UML stands for Unified Modelling language

A UML Class diagram represents the static structure of a system by showing 
its classes, attributes, methods, and relationships between classes.
It is used to help visualize the strcture of a system with its given classes.
They also show relationships between classes for example inheritance and dependency.

Used in software design and system architecture planning.
Helps in database modeling and representation of data structures.
Useful for system documentation and maintenance.
Widely used in object-oriented analysis and design.
Commonly used in enterprise and large-scale application development.

The three major sections of a UML class include;
Name 
Attributes
Operations / Methods

Attributes are represented in the second partition to show data variables

Methods are represented in the third partition to show services a class provides

Meaning of visibility symbols
+ represents public features visible to all classes
# represents protected features visible to subclasses
- represnts private features visible only within the class

An association between a class represents how different classes connect and interact with each other
with an system.

Multiplicity specifies the number of posiible values for each instance in an attribute

